From b1106e09d2dfdde9b7f0d48bceb118b942c2dfcf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michal Andrzejczak <mit.mis@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 18 Jun 2026 01:03:06 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 19/51] begonia-wifi (fwport): make consys "conn" clock
 optional (genpd powers the domain)

consys_clk_get_from_dts() aborted probe if devm_clk_get(dev,"conn") failed.
Stock bound "conn" to <&scpsys SCP_SYS_CONN> - the conn power domain expressed
as a 4.14 clock. Mainline 6.16 models conn power as genpd MT6785_POWER_DOMAIN_CONN
(power-domains is already on the consys DT node, powered by the genpd core at
probe), and the mt6785 clk driver exposes no connsys "conn" clock. Use
devm_clk_get_optional so a missing "conn" returns NULL (probe continues;
clk_prepare_enable(NULL) is a no-op) while real errors (-EPROBE_DEFER) still abort.
This clears the last probe-fatal blocker for mtk_wmt against the reconciled DT.
Verified vs stock mt6785.dts consys node (3-source: stock clocks, mainline genpd, clk driver).

Signed-off-by: Michal Andrzejczak <mit.mis@gmail.com>
---
 .../connectivity/common/common_main/platform/mt6785.c    | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/misc/mediatek/connectivity/common/common_main/platform/mt6785.c b/drivers/misc/mediatek/connectivity/common/common_main/platform/mt6785.c
index a20758e76..689545d2e 100644
--- a/drivers/misc/mediatek/connectivity/common/common_main/platform/mt6785.c
+++ b/drivers/misc/mediatek/connectivity/common/common_main/platform/mt6785.c
@@ -415,7 +415,14 @@ UINT32 mtk_wcn_consys_jtag_flag_ctrl(UINT32 en)
 
 static INT32 consys_clk_get_from_dts(struct platform_device *pdev)
 {
-	clk_scp_conn_main = devm_clk_get(&pdev->dev, "conn");
+	/* Forward-port: stock's "conn" clock was <&scpsys SCP_SYS_CONN>, i.e. the
+	 * conn power domain expressed as a 4.14 clock. Mainline 6.16 models conn
+	 * power as the genpd MT6785_POWER_DOMAIN_CONN (power-domains on the DT node),
+	 * which is powered by the genpd core at probe. There is no connsys "conn"
+	 * CLOCK to bind on mainline, so make it optional: a missing "conn" returns
+	 * NULL here, and clk_prepare_enable(NULL)/clk_disable_unprepare(NULL) are
+	 * documented no-ops downstream. Real errors (e.g. -EPROBE_DEFER) still abort. */
+	clk_scp_conn_main = devm_clk_get_optional(&pdev->dev, "conn");
 	if (IS_ERR(clk_scp_conn_main)) {
 		WMT_PLAT_PR_ERR("[CCF]cannot get clk_scp_conn_main clock.\n");
 		return PTR_ERR(clk_scp_conn_main);
-- 
